{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/1097","id":4965947325,"node_id":"PR_kwDOH8_sKs8AAAABJ_5XvQ","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/1097","diff_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/1097.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/1097.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/1097","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/1097/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/1097/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/1097/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/statuses/83dc3337b627d6d701f63e69cb77375226651947","number":1097,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix regressions from nested dict union value decoding (#1089)","user":{"login":"hramezani","id":3122442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMjI0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3122442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani","html_url":"https://github.com/hramezani","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow-up to #1089 (refs #1088). #1089 fixed decoding of union dict value types such as `dict[str, list[str] | str]`, but on unreleased main it also:\n\n- breaks plain values: `APP_CONFIG__Y=123` or `=true` for `dict[str, list[str] | str]` now fail with `Input should be a valid list`, and `\"quoted\"` loses its quotes;\n- stops decoding non-union dict values (e.g. `dict[str, list[str]]`, bare `dict`) when `enable_decoding=False`, which used to work;\n- ignores `ForceDecode` on the field containing the dict, contrary to the docs;\n- misses union value types written as type aliases or `Annotated[...]`.\n\n## Changes\n- Revert the `decode_complex_value` guard change, which restores the previous behavior for non-union dict values.\n- For union value types, only JSON arrays and objects are used. Any other value keeps the original string, as before #1089.\n- Decoding of union values follows `enable_decoding` and the `NoDecode`/`ForceDecode` of the closest field containing the dict.\n- Resolve type aliases and `Annotated` before checking the union. `Json` members are left to pydantic.\n\n## Tests\nReplaces the #1089 tests with cases on top-level dicts and dicts nested in a model: list/optional unions, `typing.Union`/`Optional`, type aliases, `Annotated`, `Json`, plain/invalid/numeric/boolean/null/quoted strings, scalar-only unions, and the `enable_decoding`/`NoDecode`/`ForceDecode` combinations.\n\nShould be merged before the next release.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01KLhWzXCi94gVGeu1tc86Vv\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-22T10:33:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T10:45:11Z","closed_at":"2026-10-22T10:45:08Z","merged_at":"2026-10-22T10:45:08Z","merge_commit_sha":"e9588aefb8a2fafa7fe7868a5aa54f24458b7497","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"pydantic:fix/1088-nested-dict-union-decodin